    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d930">

                <pb facs="0872" n="782" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg782"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 860d.00/102</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the British Ambassador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Reading</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-04-20"><hi rendition="#italic">April 20,
                        1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Ambassador</hi>: I have received a report
                    from the American Minister at Stockholm dated April 19, 1918, giving the text of
                    a memorandum handed that day by the Minister of Great Britain at Stockholm to
                    the Finnish Chargé d’Affaires to the effect that the British Government is
                    prepared to recognize provisionally the <hi rendition="#italic">de facto</hi>
                    independence of Finland, pending final settlement of the question by the peace
                    congress, in accordance with the principle of self-determination, provided
                    certain conditions are complied with.</p>
                <p>The American Minister at Stockholm has been informed that this Government is not
                    prepared at present to take any action looking to the independence of Finland,
                    and I have thought that you will be interested to know our attitude.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert
                                Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
